<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3 BCE–<a href="/years/69">69 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Servius Sulpicius Galba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galba was a Roman senator who, as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Tarraconensis, was proclaimed emperor by his troops in 68 CE during the revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a>. He became emperor after Nero's suicide, the first of the Year of the Four Emperors. His severity and refusal to pay the Praetorian Guard cost him support, and he was murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in January 69.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galba.jpg" alt="Galba" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: American Numismatic Society · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_Aureus_of_Galba_(MANTIS).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
